# AFTERBELL reference-data configuration.
# Copy to .env. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# The default provider is Yahoo, which needs no key and no account, so a
# default install holds no credential anywhere. Leave this file empty and the
# reference side works.
#
# REFERENCE_PROVIDER=yahoo        # yahoo (default) | alpaca
#
# Alpaca is optional and only worth configuring if you want the reference to
# come from the firm that clears the shares behind these tokens. Note that
# Alpaca issues no read-only credential: a key that fetches a price can also
# place an order, and its rate limits are shared across every application using
# that account. Prefer a paper key, and never one already in use elsewhere.
# ALPACA_API_KEY=
# ALPACA_SECRET_KEY=

# Binance market data requires NO credentials (Law 10). The recorder holds
# no token by design and cannot die from OAuth expiry. Do not add one here.
